restart the server

1->docker compose up -d --build

or 

2-> docker compose restart backend


1) docker compose ps

2)docker compose exec backend alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Initial tables"

3) docker-compose exec backend alembic upgrade head
4) docker compose down

redis -> ensures that everyone on the chatroom gets the same message regardless of which server they are on like if a person sends message on container A then container B and C also gets the same message


# to run the database

-> docker compose exec db psql -U user -d translate_app

# enter container 
-> docker compose exec backend bash

# recreate containers
docker compose down
docker compose up --build

# creating the frontend with zustand and tailwind css

npx create-next-app@14 frontend --typescript --tailwind --eslint --app --src-dir --import-alias "@/*"
>> cd frontend
>> npm install zustand

#stop a docker
-> docker compose down

# start the frontend
-> cd frontend
-> npm run dev


# install and setup expo for android

-> npx create-expo-app@latest mobile
-> cd mobile
-> npx expo install expo-secure-store react-native-screens react-native-safe-area-context @react-navigation/native @react-navigation/native-stack zustand


# llm models 
-> qwen for translation 

# how to load llm 
-> ollama run qwen2.5:3b

# how to run the project 
-> ollama run qwen2.5:3b
1) docker compose up -d --build 
1) or docker compose start

Apply database updates (only needed once):

2) docker compose exec backend alembic revision --autogenerate -m "setup_database"
3) docker compose exec backend alembic upgrade head

Start the Web Frontend
on another teminal
4) cd frontend
5) npm run dev

6) Open your browser and go to http://localhost:3000

Start the Mobile App
on another teminal
7) cd mobile
8) npx expo start

Press a to launch the Android Emulator, or scan the QR code using the Expo Go app on your phone.

